# Actions and blocks, by the rulebook's own examples (vekn.net/rulebook, "Game Setup", "Minion
# Phase", "Bleed", "Hunt", "Who May Attempt to Block") and zero-vtes docs/rules-qa.md (24.4).
# Sarah plays first; her prey is Alexis, her predator Pieter.
seed 5
seat S sarah
seat X alexis
seat P pieter
crypt S "Vera Nightfall" *12
library S "Iron Ward" *40
crypt X "Tomas Grey" *12
library X "Quick Feed" *40
crypt P "Ilse Várga" *12
library P "Gate Hound" *40
start

# Game Setup: 30 pool each, 7 cards in hand, 4 crypt cards in the uncontrolled region, and the
# Edge in the centre, nobody's.
expect pool S 30
expect pool X 30
expect count S:hand 7
expect count S:uncontrolled 4
expect edge none

S> move S:uncontrolled:1 ready
S> move S:uncontrolled:1 ready
X> move X:uncontrolled:1 ready
P> move P:uncontrolled:1 ready
S> transfer +2 S:ready:1
S> next
S> next
expect turn 1 S minion

# "Belinde bleeds Alexis for 1": a bleed is directed at the prey, and only the target may block.
# Unblocked and for 1 or more, it succeeds and Sarah takes the Edge.
S> bleed S:ready:1
expect action bleed S blocks
reject P> block P:ready:1
X> pass
S> resolve success 1 edge
expect pool X 29
expect edge S
S> pass
expect action none

# Only unlocked minions act. You can never bleed yourself: naming your own seat bleeds the prey.
reject S> bleed S:ready:1
S> bleed S:ready:2 S
log public S: Vera Nightfall bleeds X
S> cancel
S> unlock S:ready:2

# "The Dowager recruits the Underbridge Stray": undirected, so the prey and the predator may
# block, the prey first. Alexis declines, and that decision is final; then Pieter may block.
S> recruit S:ready:2 with S:hand:1
expect action recruit S blocks
expect impulse X
X> pass
reject X> block X:ready:1
expect impulse P
P> block P:ready:1
S> pass
P> pass
expect action recruit S combat
S> endcombat
S> pass
expect action none

# A blocker must be ready and unlocked: Ilse, locked by her block, can't block again.
S> unlock S:ready:1
S> hunt S:ready:1
X> pass
reject P> block P:ready:1
P> pass
# Hunt: the vampire gains 1 blood (Vera: 2 → 3).
S> resolve success
expect card S:ready:1 blood 3

# zero-vtes 24.4: a bleed is successful only for 1 or more; a bleed of 0 takes no Edge.
S> edge none
S> unlock S:ready:1
S> bleed S:ready:1
X> pass
S> resolve success 0 edge
expect pool X 29
expect edge none
